esults. Call `ki_search(query='render protocol measurement __rich_console__ __rich_measure__ segments', page=2)` (or `offset=5`) to view more.*"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_search"},"structuredContent":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 21 result(s) for \"render protocol measurement __rich_console__ __rich_measure__ segments\" [Page 1/5 (showing 1-5)]:\n\n> 💡 **Next page**: `ki_search(query=\"render protocol measurement __rich_console__ __rich_measure__ segments\", page=2)` (or `offset=5`)\n\n1. [KI] **ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md`, score: 7.66)\n   > # ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Rich supports...\n2. [KI] **ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation** (`.ki-base/decisions/0002-render-protocol.md`, score: 7.66)\n   > # ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Rich supports...\n3. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Markdown, Markup, Panels & Prompts)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_markdown.md`, score: 5.835)\n   > <!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Markdown, Markup, Panels & Prompts) ## Overview Provides markdown document parsing, console markup parsing (`[bold red]...[/]`), framed panel...\n4. [KI] **KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts)** (`.ki-base/knowledge/KI_rich_align.md`, score: 5.382)\n   > <!-- last_verified: 2026-11-08 --> # KI: Rich Core (Console, Alignment & Core Layouts) ## Overview Central pipeline of Rich: houses the primary `Console` class, ANSI escape sequence decoder, cell...\n5. [KI] **ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition** (`.ki-base/decisions/0001-terminal-segments.md`, score: 5.194)\n   > # ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition - **Status:** Accepted - **Date:** 2026-11-08 - **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers ## Context Terminal emulators...\n\n*Showing 5 of 21 results. Call `ki_search(query='render protocol measurement __rich_console__ __rich_measure__ segments', page=2)` (or `offset=5`) to view more.*"}]}},"isError":false,"durationMs":106}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"toolu_01TUCy1kPL1HqgvTqY61W43Y","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"structuredContent":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0002: Render Protocol & Component Isolation\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nRich supports arbitrary nested UI components (such as Panels inside Tables inside Trees). If custom components were allowed to mutate shared rendering options or directly manipulate the `Console` buffer, rendering would become non-deterministic, thread-unsafe, and incompatible with real-time displays like `Live` and `Progress`.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Mandatory Console Protocol:**  \n   All visual components must implement the public generator protocol:\n   ```python\n   def __rich_console__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> \"RenderResult\":\n       ...\n       yield Segment(...)\n   ```\n   A component may optionally implement `__rich_measure__(self, console: \"Console\", options: \"ConsoleOptions\") -> Measurement` for dynamic sizing.\n\n2. **Strict Component Isolation Invariants:**\n   - **No Buffer Access:** Components must NEVER access or write to `console._buffer` or `console.file` directly. All output must be returned via `yield` as an iterable of `Segment` or renderable objects.\n   - **Options Immutability:** The passed `options: ConsoleOptions` instance is strictly read-only. Components must never mutate its fields. To adjust constraints for child components, use `options.update(...)` which returns a fresh copy.\n   - **Stateless Yielding:** Generators must be re-entrant and idempotent so that multiple render passes (e.g. measuring then rendering) produce identical results without side effects.\n\n3. **Internal Spacing Convention for Inline Badges:**\n   - In accordance with repository design conventions, inline badge components must enclose their inner text with exactly one space of padding inside the boundary caps: `\"( \"` + content + `\" )\"` for pill badges, and `\"[\" + \" \"` + content + `\" ]\"` for square badges.\n   - Example: `Badge(\"DEPLOYED\", pill=True, icon=\"★\")` must yield segments rendering as `\"( ★ DEPLOYED )\"`. Square badges render as `\"[ SYSTEM ALERT ]\"`. Measurement must include the 4 cells occupied by borders and inner spaces.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Components can be composed arbitrarily without side effects.\n- Direct console buffer writes or mutating shared options is treated as an architectural violation and rejected in code review.\n- Ensures seamless integration with `Live` displays and virtual screen buffers.\n"}]}},"isError":false,"durationMs":121}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"toolu_01NFes1KFpqez5ngtapfjDhK","toolName":"mcp__ki_manager__ki_read","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n"}],"details":{"server":"ki-manager","tool":"ki_read"},"structuredContent":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ADR-0001: Terminal Segments & Atomic Decomposition\n\n- **Status:** Accepted\n- **Date:** 2026-11-08\n- **Deciders:** Rich Architectural Maintainers\n\n## Context\n\nTerminal emulators operate on streams of characters interspersed with ANSI escape codes for styling and cursor movement. Without a unified primitive abstraction, high-level components (tables, syntax, markdown) would have to manually track escape codes, calculate visual cell widths, and handle cross-platform line breaks, leading to exponential complexity and bugs.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Atomic Segment Primitive:**  \n   Every visual element in Rich must ultimately reduce to a stream of `Segment` instances:\n   ```python\n   class Segment(NamedTuple):\n       text: str\n       style: Optional[Style] = None\n       control: Optional[Sequence[ControlCode]] = None\n   ```\n2. **Strict Invariants:**\n   - A `Segment` text piece must not contain unescaped newline characters `\\n` or `\\r` unless processed by `Segment.split_lines()` or `Segment.split_and_crop_lines()`.\n   - Visual measurement is derived strictly from `cell_len(segment.text)` using East Asian Width Unicode tables, never raw `len(text)`.\n   - Control sequences (cursor up, color palette queries) are encapsulated in the optional `control` field and take zero visual cell length.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- All rendering operations are stateless stream-processing pipelines.\n- Layout algorithms only need to measure and slice `Segment` collections.\n- Clean separation between logical layout calculation and physical terminal escape emission.\n"}]}},"isError":false,"durationMs":133}
